# ORCLPUSH: the push family — boulders and both sliders (M16.4).
#
# ElementPushablePush (ELEMENTS.PAS) is one recursive procedure covering three
# separate decisions, and this scenario separates them:
#
#   1. is the touched tile pushable at all — a boulder always is, an NS slider
#      only when deltaX is 0, an EW slider only when deltaY is 0;
#   2. what sits behind it — the push recurses into a chain, and only completes
#      when the far end lands on a walkable tile;
#   3. what happens to an unwalkable blocker — it is damaged away only when it
#      is Destructible, which a gem is and a breakable wall is not.
#
# The player runs down a clear highway at x=3 and steps east into one station
# per stop, then crosses to two stations that are pushed vertically. Refusals
# are checkpointed as deliberately as the successes: ElementPushableTouch queues
# its click whether or not the push lands, so a refused station is an audible
# click over an unchanged board, not a no-op.
world ORCLPUSH
seed 0
boot 240
capture title
play
# unpause and walk down the highway to the first station
move down
move down
# A: lone boulder with empty ground behind it — boulder 4->5, player 3->4
move right
capture push-boulder
move left
move down
move down
# B: boulder backed by solid — nothing is pushable behind it, so the push is
# refused and the player stays put
move right
capture refuse-boulder
move down
move down
# C: boulder chain ending in empty — the recursion advances both boulders
move right
capture push-chain
move left
move down
move down
# D: boulder backed by a breakable wall — breakable is neither pushable nor
# Destructible, so the chain refuses and the wall survives intact
move right
capture refuse-breakable
move down
move down
# E: boulder backed by a gem — a gem IS Destructible, so it is crushed rather
# than collected (Gems stays 0) and the boulder takes its square
move right
capture crush-gem
move left
move down
move down
# F: NS slider pushed east — off-axis, so it refuses
move right
capture refuse-slider-ns
move down
move down
# G: EW slider pushed east — on-axis, so it slides
move right
capture push-slider-ew
# cross to the vertical stations along row 19
move down
move right
move right
move right
move right
# H: NS slider pushed south — on-axis, so it slides
move down
capture push-slider-ns
move up
move right
move right
move right
move right
# I: EW slider pushed south — off-axis, so it refuses
move down
capture refuse-slider-ew
